      "updated_at": "2026-11-03T18:41:42+00:00",
      "author": "Gabriel Coler",
      "product_type": "summary",
      "bottom_line": "<p>I often make the joke that Bend is never as excited about backcountry riding as when there is 6 inches of snow on the cinder cone!&nbsp; Sure enough there is snow in the high country and folks have been getting out sliding around.&nbsp; The Central Oregon Avalanche Center is scheduled to begin daily avalanche forecasting on December 1.&nbsp; By no means does this mean that avalanches aren't possible before then.&nbsp; If you are headed out to make turns or ride in avalanche terrain, you should consider the possibility of avalanches.&nbsp; This means doing all the same things you should be doing later in the winter:&nbsp; carrying avalanche rescue gear, using thoughtful travel techniques, and assessing the snowpack.&nbsp; When the snow is shallow, folks might be looking for where it's blown in a bit to hit the least rocks.&nbsp; These wind blown deposits can also be the most likely places to find significant avalanches during the early season.&nbsp; If you are thinking about heading out, check out both our <a href=\"https://coavalanche.org/pages/observations#/view/observations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">observations</a> page as well as our <a href=\"https://coavalanche.org/pages/weather-map#/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">weather station map</a> for conditions.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Hopefully the snow will continue to pile up, and we'll have great riding by the time we begin operating.&nbsp; In the meantime, be careful out there; of avalanches, but maybe more so of rocks, logs and other snow snakes.&nbsp; Be patient.&nbsp; Snow is exciting, but even our worst winters are long.&nbsp; The avalanche center has lots of pre-season events scheduled to help you build enthusiasm for the season!&nbsp; Here is a link to our events page: &nbsp;<a href=\"https://coavalanche.org/pages/events\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://coavalanche.org/pages/events</a>.</p>",
